    <body>
      <div xml:id="gom-sir37">
        <head xml:id="gom-sir37-Hd1e98">Caput 37</head>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir37-Dd1e100">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir37-Hd1e102">Versus 1</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir37-d1e104">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e106" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir37_1@1-2">Omnis amicus.</quote>
            <ref xml:id="gom-sir37-Rd1e109"><name xml:id="gom-sir37-Nd1e110" ref="#RabanusMaurus">RAB.</name></ref>
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e113">Superius diligentius expressit verum amicum et falsum, dicens: <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e115" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir6_8@7-12">Et non permanebit in die tribulationis.</quote></quote>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir37-Dd1e120">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir37-Hd1e122">Versus 2</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir37-d1e124">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e126" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir37_2@1-2">Sodalis autem.</quote>
            Verus amicus toto animo diligit, et opere proficit. Unde, <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e129" source="http://scta.info/resource/Iio3_18@2-10">Non diligamus verbo neque lingua, sed opere et veritate</quote>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir37-Dd1e134">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir37-Hd1e136">Versus 3</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir37-d1e138">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e140" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir37_3@1-2">O Praesumptio.</quote>
            Detestatur hypocrisim, <pb ed="#P" n="1219D"/> cum malus se bonum esse simulat <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e145" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir37_3@7-9">cooperiendo aridam malitiam,</quote> in qua scilicet non est pinguedo charitatis vel misericordiae.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir37-Dd1e150">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir37-Hd1e152">Versus 5</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir37-d1e154">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e156" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir37_5@4-5">Causa ventris.</quote>
            Pro gula, non pro amicitia. Possuntt in falsis amicis haeretici intelligi, qui omnia recte faciunt, quasi animarum consultores, cum sint proditores. Unde, <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e159" source="http://scta.info/resource/mt7_15@1-5">Attendite a falsis prophetis qui</quote>, etc.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir37-Dd1e165">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir37-Hd1e167">Versus 7</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir37-d1e169">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e171" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir37_7@3-4">Cum socero.</quote>
            Socer, qui a parte feminea est cognatus, muliebrem et mutabilem ostendit animum, similiter et zelus qui praecipue est animarum.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir37-Dd1e176">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir37-Hd1e178">Versus 8</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir37-d1e180">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e182" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir37_8@1-2">Omnis consiliarius.</quote>
            Adhuc docet cautelam omnem habendam in suscipiendis amicis et consiliariis. Multi enim se amicos et consiliarios fingunt, <pb ed="#P" n="1220A"/> et insidias tendunt. Unde Jeremias, <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e187" source="http://scta.info/resource/ier9_4@1-6">Unusquisque se a proximo suo custodiat</quote>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir37-Dd1e192">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir37-Hd1e194">Versus 14</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir37-d1e196">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e198" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir37_14">Non attendite.</quote>
            <!-- check: lemma not matched to verse text -->
            <ref xml:id="gom-sir37-Rd1e203"><name xml:id="gom-sir37-Nd1e204" ref="#RabanusMaurus">RAB.</name></ref>
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e207">Diversas species consiliantium enumeravit, in quibus plures personas notavit, quae a veritate discordant. Unde praecepit cum talibus non esse consiliandum, quorum consilium periclitatur. Praevidenda est ergo consiliarii prudentia, fides, voluntas, et religio.</quote>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir37-Dd1e211">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir37-Hd1e213">Versus 18</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir37-d1e215">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e217" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir37_18@1-3">Anima sancti viri.</quote>
            Consiliariorum, diversitate ostensa, adjungit, quantum humanae sapientiae sanctorum excellat scientia a Spiritu sancto infusa.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir37-Dd1e222">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir37-Hd1e224">Versus 22</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir37-d1e226">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e228" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir37_22@1-2">Vir peritus.</quote>
            Quia de lingua praedixerat: de bonis malisque doctoribus continuat.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir37-Dd1e233">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir37-Hd1e235">Versus 28</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir37-d1e237">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e239" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir37_28@1-2">Vita viri.</quote>
            <ref xml:id="gom-sir37-Rd1e242"><name xml:id="gom-sir37-Nd1e243" ref="#RabanusMaurus">ID.</name></ref>
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e246">Praesens vita hominum <pb ed="#P" n="1220B"/> in incerto non est apud eum. Unde, <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e250" source="http://scta.info/resource/iob14_5@1-10">Breves dies hominis sunt, numerus mensium apud te est</quote>.</quote>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir37-Dd1e257">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir37-Hd1e259">Versus 32</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir37-d1e261">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e263" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir37_32@1-2">Noli avidus.</quote>
            Juxta historiam, parcimoniam laudat, crapulam vituperat, quae ad infirmitatem perducit devorantem. Mystice vero admonet, ut in temporalibus simus temperantes. Unde, <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e266" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov25_16@1-6">Mel invenisti, comede quod sufficit tibi</quote>, etc. Et alibi: <quote xml:id="gom-sir37-Qd1e269" source="http://scta.info/resource/rom12_3@14-18">Non plus sapere quam oportet</quote>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </body>
